sification-symbol></classification-ecla><invention-title load-source="docdb"  status="new" lang="EN">INK-JET RECORDER</invention-title><invention-title load-source="docdb" status="new" lang="FR">DISPOSITIF D'ENREGISTREMENT RELATIF AU JET D'ENCRE</invention-title><citations><patent-citations><patcit ucid="JP-10006527-A" status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>10006527</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source name="APP"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8174863-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8174863</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id> <sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit> </patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1038682A1</text><sources><source name="APP" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEINO TAKEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEINO, TAKEO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEINO TAKEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEINO, TAKEO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>When ink cartridges (1, 2) are detached and loaded, the type of the loaded ink cartridges (1, 2) is identified based on the ID data and data on the amount of ink stored in storage means (32, 42). If the cartridges are new, a small amount of ink is sucked; contrarily if the cartridges are reloaded by mistake by the user, a relatively large amount of ink is sucked. Thus the consumption of ink during ink-filling accompanying the loading of the ink cartridges (1, 2) is reduced while maintaining the printing quality.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Selon l'invention, lors de l'enlèvement et du chargement de cartouches d'encre (1, 2), le type des cartouches (1, 2) est identifié en fonction de données d'identification et de données relatives à la quantité d'encre, conservées dans des moyens de stockage (32, 42). Si les cartouches sont neuves, une petite quantité d'encre est aspirée; au contraire, si les cartouches sont rechargées par erreur par l'utilisateur, une quantité relativement grande est aspirée. Ainsi, on réduit la consommation d'encre lors du remplissage d'encre accompagnant le chargement des cartouches d'encre (1, 2), tout en maintenant la qualité d'impression.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>